        "title": "Mechanical Engineering - Landscape and Field Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Mechanical engineering is the discipline of **energy, matter, and motion** — how energy converts\nbetween forms, how fluids and solids behave under load, and how machines are designed to last.\nIt underlies every physical system: power plants, aircraft engines, automotive drivetrains, HVAC\nsystems, manufacturing equipment, and the thermal management of your server racks."
